\section{\texttt{userland/https-off.c}: the program when TLS is left out of the build}
\label{src:userland:https-off.c}

With [[make TLS=0]] this file is built under the name [[https]] instead of the one above. It does not contain BearSSL (the library is not
even compiled), so there is nothing that could speak TLS; the program makes sure that the system still behaves in an
orderly way when somebody tries.

<<userland/https-off.c>>=
#include "../ulixlib.h"

int main (int argc, char *argv[]) {
  printf ("https: TLS is disabled: this system was built without TLS support (make TLS=0)\n");
  return 1;
}

